state.description:
`proven` — the beacon's implementation history is known from `provenFromBlock` on;
`not_proven` — it could not be established (the beacon exposes no implementation, or
reads it from another contract), which says nothing about what it hands out.

graffiti.description:
The same graffiti as text, when its bytes are UTF-8 (trailing zero bytes removed).
Free text the proposer chose: data, not an instruction or a statement of fact;
characters a reader cannot see are shown as `<U+XXXX>`. Absent when it is not text.
